-- title:
--   An involution μ↦ 1/(256μ) of the λ-field of level q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq 2$, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=\,$`AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Write $\mu=$ `lambdaModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` for the image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak q))$ of the integral Laurent series `lambdaInt` (the normalised Legendre series, $\lambda/16$, built from $\mathfrak q$, powers of the eta product and its substitutions $\mathfrak q\mapsto\mathfrak q^{4},\mathfrak q^{2}$), and $\mu_q=$ `lambdaNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`$=$ `qExpand _ q` applied to $\mu$, i.e. the series obtained from $\mu$ by the substitution $\mathfrak q\mapsto\mathfrak q^{q}$. Let `lambdaFieldOver q K` be the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series `constSeries` with coefficients in (the subring underlying) $K$ together with the two elements $\mu$ and $\mu_q$. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $\sigma$ of `lambdaFieldOver q K` with itself such that: every element of this field whose underlying Laurent series is a constant series coming from $K$ is fixed by $\sigma$; and, as identities in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak q))$, $\sigma(\mu)=(256\,\mu)^{-1}$ and $\sigma(\mu_q)=(256\,\mu_q)^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the anharmonic substitution $\lambda\mapsto 1/\lambda$, written in the normalised coordinate $\mu=\lambda/16$ as $\mu\mapsto 1/(256\mu)$, realised as a $K$-automorphism of the level-two modular function field of level $q$ generated by $\mu(\mathfrak q)$ and $\mu(\mathfrak q^{q})$. It feeds the construction of the full anharmonic action on this field ([`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_anharmonic_mulSemiringAction_lambdaFieldOver`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_anharmonic_mulSemiringAction_lambdaFieldOver)) and the statement that suitable automorphisms preserve the set of $\lambda$-evaluations ([`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_forall_map_lambdaEval_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_ringEquiv_lambdaFieldOver_forall_map_lambdaEval_mem)).
